<section class="section" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Scaling questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How many stores and terminals can the platform handle?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The platform runs across more than 30,000 terminals in over 40 countries at 99.99% uptime. Our largest single-customer deployment is a global apparel retailer running more than 2,500 stores across 25-plus markets on one platform. Deployments range from that international fleet down to single-venue and pop-up operations on the same system.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What happens when we expand into a new country?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Fiscal compliance is built into the platform for more than 40 countries, covering requirements such as VAT, GST, NF525, and TSE, with multi-currency and multi-language configured per market. Regional payment methods are handled natively, including integrated merchant platforms, QR-based mobile wallets, and market-specific flows such as digital invoicing in China and installment selection in South Korea. Entering a market is a configuration exercise rather than a separate implementation with a local vendor.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What happens at peak volume, or when the network drops?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Store-and-Forward keeps every terminal fully operational during a network outage, encrypting transactions locally on the device and syncing automatically when connectivity returns. For throughput, RFID self-checkout completes a basket in 30 seconds or less with no item-by-item scanning, and terminals can be added or removed as demand moves.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Can we customize workflows without getting stuck on an old version?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Custom services integrate through external APIs and logic overlays without altering the core POS codebase, and the interface itself is configurable, module sequence, order, and exposure are set per retailer. Because the capability set runs on one codebase rather than a collection of integrations, there is a single upgrade path instead of a regression cycle for every connected app.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How quickly can new staff be productive as we grow?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Role-based training is assigned automatically from the team member record, with course material synchronized from live product data so associates learn the current assortment. In practice, the iOS interface brings associate training to under 30 minutes, and the Colorado Rockies put new seasonal associates on registers within five minutes of starting.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

